  "summary": "Haitian metal sculpture tradition using recycled oil drums cut and shaped into intricate forms.",
  "description": "Features intricate, three-dimensional sculptures crafted from recycled oil drums, with distinctive blackened surfaces and detailed relief work depicting religious, historical, and everyday subjects. This craft evolved from the metalworking traditions of African slaves in Haiti, transformed by the availability of discarded oil barrels in the mid-20th century.",
